    body: "The video for Sabrina Carpenter's \"Taste,\" the lead single from her album _Short n' Sweet_, holds a special place in the singer's cinematic universe largely thanks to her co-star Jenna Ortega. The unkillable duo chase each other with machetes, rifles, and chainsaws in a wildly campy send-up of classics like _Death Becomes Her_.\n\nGiven how many times they kill each other over the course of the three-minute clip, fans might assume this bloody spectacle took weeks to plan. In reality, Ortega revealed she only found out she'd be involved in the shoot a few days beforehand.\n\n\"I swear, none of that video was choreographed. We were just running around. We didn't have time to prep or talk about it,\" Ortega told _Esquire_. The actress pointed to the scene where she kisses her boyfriend, who then transforms into Carpenter, as an example; in that scene Ortega saws Carpenter in half with a pink chainsaw.\n\n\"The kissing sequence was: I was standing there, kissing a guy. They told me not to break position. Sabrina comes in, kisses me, and we did that a few times,\" Ortega recalled. \"So it was kind of like a lovers' carousel.\"\n\nAsked about her favorite scene with Carpenter, the _Wednesday_ star's answer was clear: \"The chainsaw sequence. It just felt so campy and fun, and we were wearing cute outfits, too.\" Ortega added that even the chainsaw had a wild name that referenced Carpenter.",
