    body: "Avenged Sevenfold guitarist Zacky Vengeance has had a hand in some of modern metal's most iconic songs. But the guitarist doesn't only listen to heavy music — far from it.\n\nVengeance, born Zachary Baker, recently released his debut solo album, 'Dark Horse.' The record reveals the artist's love for old-school country, rockabilly, and more.\n\nIn this list for Revolver, Baker picks out and discusses 11 non-metal albums, ranging from Weezer to Lana Del Rey, that he believes every metalhead absolutely needs to hear. The list serves as a kind of crossover guide meant to broaden the heavy-music listener's palate: records that show how melody, production, and songwriting operate regardless of genre.\n\nYou can watch the full list in Revolver's video series.",
